han 24 hours from ohio to newfoundland  and labrador at age 85. but shirley  brooks jones is determined to keep  saying thank you to the people of gander  and surrounding communities i mean they  didn't have to do what they did for us  they could have just looked the other  way they could have said oh well  somebody else can take care of them you  know but they didn't  shirley and almost 7 000 other  passengers were stranded in the gander  area after the 9 11 terrorist attacks  those newfoundlanders  were absolutely awesome they opened  their hearts their homes their their  churches their service clubs i mean  in a few days  we fell in love with him we we truly did  for 20 years the love affair has  continued  shirley has made dozens of trips back to  gander and lewisport to hand out the  flight 15 scholarship from a fund she  initiated  a smile on her face i wanted all times  into the future  for the people of that area to know  that we would never forget what they had  done for us  live  hundreds of high school students have  qualified for the scholarship including  raylene kirby on her path to becoming a  family doctor i don't know shirley will  ever know  what a role model she's been in my life  as a strong female  leader and  just a beautiful person overall they're  eating the sleeping in the same area  shirley's best friends in lewisport bill  and thelma hooper are excited to see her  again she's just one of our family now  really as a concession to covert 19 this  visit is different i've already told her  that no  we're not allowed not supposed to hog  or even shake hands for surely it's hard  to hold back eventually i'm going to  touch your arm or your face or your or  something else but hugging that's  something you know if you're if things  are good or bad or whatever hugs and not  being able to hug it just about kills  you but even the pandemic doesn't dampen  her enthusiasm for giving back i love  those people i love them even when i die  i'll love them 